ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3ed1f6f620e130ecb14a0a65ec7864d61a0ea0f80a4ab5e1c9696f9f9a3fc9f4","event_uuid":"8fce1cbb-5a31-49c9-bb2e-60259b48853d","position":{"commit_sha":"2087d7eaca70fb85234253224874ae8fd0f6025b","position":"1786601027994730001-8fce1cbb-5a31-49c9-bb2e-60259b48853d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8f1d6a53a2efb3cca05edae31ce9ed6d6e54556b1c8f9bc70216a0668102fef3","event_uuid":"902aa29c-4990-4818-b898-9b0145bf9248","position":{"commit_sha":"cdf67e0b1b1994891f1b75eddb39f5a04f8bf09c","position":"1786601036219887001-902aa29c-4990-4818-b898-9b0145bf9248"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Closing as a duplicate: `bloated-shadeful-lamprey` (4631-5598-7127-4a56) already covers taking `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` off the module-size cap, with a concrete seam (the `_python_leaf` mutation block -> `_lib_mutations.py`). Filed from `defaceable-icy-antelope` before that ticket surfaced in search.\n\nTwo facts worth carrying over to the surviving ticket: `_lib_writes.py` has since grown from the 778 LOC its plan records to **exactly 800**, so it is now AT the cap rather than approaching it; and six further files sit at 798-799 (`llm/workflow/completion_banking.py`, `llm/plan_review/pass1.py`, `_store/push.py`, `signing.py`, `_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py`, `llm/structured_run.py` at 796).","timestamp":1786600994270487001}],"created_at":1786600951857937001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"04b06d7d-6c02-4073-a3b9-df30dedd744d","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"4631-5598-7127-4a56"}],"description":"# `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` is at exactly 800/800 LOC\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nSurfaced while reworking the fsck cluster on `defaceable-icy-antelope`. With `fsck.py` taken\noff the cap, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` is now the largest file in `src/rebar` at **exactly\n800** — the hard cap in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`, enforced by the CI module-size gate\nwith no allowlist. The next change to it of any size, including a one-line bug fix, cannot land.\n\nThis is the fourth instance of the pattern (`valiant-balladic-willet` did `passes.py`,\n`splurgy-witless-flamingo` did `_ref_lock.py`, `defaceable-icy-antelope` did `fsck.py`), and\nseveral more files are within a handful of lines:\n\n| file | LOC |\n|---|---|\n| src/rebar/_lib_writes.py | 800 |\n| src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py | 799 |\n| src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py | 799 |\n| src/rebar/_store/push.py | 799 |\n| src/rebar/signing.py | 798 |\n| src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py | 798 |\n\n## Approach\n\nFollow the pattern set by `defaceable-icy-antelope`: take an architectural view rather than a\nmechanical split. Identify the actual concerns in the module, then extract along a call-graph\nseam that already exists — a helper family with a single internal call site is the seam a prior\nauthor cut and stopped at. Name each new module for its concern. Target 200-500 LOC per file;\nnever create a module under 100 LOC (if a candidate concern is smaller, it belongs with its\nnearest collaborator). Behaviour-preserving: identical behaviour, identical exit codes.\n\nRead the architectural-analysis comment on `defaceable-icy-antelope` first — it records the\nconcern-map method, the re-export compatibility constraint for module-attribute callers, and\nthe complexity-ratchet re-keying that any move requires.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` is at most 500 lines — verified by\n      `[ \"$(wc -l < src/rebar/_lib_writes.py)\" -le 500 ]` exiting 0.\n- [ ] AC2: each new module is at least 100 lines — verified by `wc -l` on each.\n- [ ] AC3: no `src/rebar` file exceeds the hard cap — verified by\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` exiting 0.\n- [ ] AC4: no test file is edited — verified by `git diff --stat origin/main -- tests/`\n      producing no output.\n- [ ] AC5: `make lint`, `make typecheck` and `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n      each exit 0.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"902aa29c-4990-4818-b898-9b0145bf9248","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"287a-2be7-acba-426a","ticket_type":"task","title":"_lib_writes.py sits at exactly 800/800 LOC — the next file pinned at the cap","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fe234d47-c27e-41c3-b401-3b03d33511da","04b06d7d-6c02-4073-a3b9-df30dedd744d","c549be48-7216-4e94-b26a-63c5f8da15f5","8fce1cbb-5a31-49c9-bb2e-60259b48853d","902aa29c-4990-4818-b898-9b0145bf9248"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659543384786001,"uuid":"c730a838-90cf-4519-9466-ce52dcc35d7f"}